/**
 * src/db/seed.ts — `npm run db:seed`
 *
 * A demo portfolio for a mid-market property manager: three properties, eight
 * vendors, and a certificate file in every state the product has to handle —
 * compliant, expiring, deficient, expired, awaiting review, a parse that failed,
 * and a vendor with nothing on file at all.
 *
 * Every certificate is a real PDF, generated by lib/acord-sample.ts and run through
 * the actual intake path, so the review queue, the PDF viewer and the binder export
 * all have genuine documents behind them. Dates are relative to today, so the demo
 * stays sensible whenever it is run.
 *
 * Safe to re-run: it deletes the demo org and everything under it first, and it
 * refuses to touch a database that has any other org in it.
 */

